<section image-layout="blank" id="cLCtn87nOc"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="jPfzkGcBON" vertical-align="center" colspan="36"><p role="eyebrow">Illustrative replacement · 12 ha field</p><h1 font-size="48pt">The gap is five hours</h1><p font-size="lg">At 2.0 m and 5.0 km/h, field losses turn a theoretical 12.00-hour job into 17.14 hours of work.</p><spacer size="16pt"></spacer><grid divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="j92SNizWFh" colspan="20"><display size="md">1.00</display><h4>ha/hour theoretical</h4><p font-size="sm">Width and speed, before losses.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="AmqtddgU7_" colspan="20"><display size="md">0.70</display><h4>ha/hour effective</h4><p font-size="sm">At 70% field efficiency.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="f9Tc0U4dEk" colspan="20"><display size="md"><span text-color="accent">5.14</span></display><h4>hours added</h4><p font-size="sm">The gap to explain and reduce.</p></grid-item></grid><spacer size="14pt"></spacer><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="v90pTIuC2A" background-color="accent" padding="12pt 16pt"><h4>Efficiency begins by explaining that 5.14-hour gap.</h4></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">The source document was not supplied; all examples in this deck are created and illustrative.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="yfwgVSha_0" padding="0" colspan="24"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/QWf0hE26o8zs8fyLshCqG.png" saved-media-id="mgmujrrp5hvers2" source="image.ai-generated" fill="true" image-style="technical-field-documentary" alt="Elevated documentary photograph of an unbranded compact tractor working a rectangular cultivated field, parallel passes and a broad headland clearly visible, neutral overcast daylight, realistic soil texture, carbon-black and machine-gray equipment with one restrained signal-red marker, no text, no logos, no identifiable people" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="7bHrCxXJRG"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="TU7Y--B-hM"><h2>Three numbers define field efficiency</h2><p>The recurring example starts with three operating inputs. Keep their units fixed and enter efficiency as a decimal.</p><grid divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="i4uPHpeWEh" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><display size="md">2.0<span font-size="20pt"> m</span></display><h4>Working width</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="kUsimZOQCz" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><display size="md">5.0<span font-size="20pt"> km/h</span></display><h4>Operating speed</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="ysJ4ZjS3sV" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><display size="md"><span text-color="accent">0.70</span></display><h4>Field efficiency</h4></grid-item></grid><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="ocr1kI96Mq" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><h3>Capacity ladder</h3><p role="eyebrow">Theoretical capacity</p><formula>C_t=\frac{2.0\times5.0}{10}=1.00\ \text{ha/hour}</formula><p role="eyebrow">Effective capacity</p><formula>C_e=C_t\times0.70=0.70\ \text{ha/hour}</formula></grid-item><grid-item id="6NFDkfAgt8" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><h3>Losses become cost</h3><formula>\eta_f=\frac{C_e}{C_t}=0.70</formula><p>Field efficiency captures turning, overlap, refilling, adjustment and stoppage losses.</p><formula>\frac{\$54/\text{hour}}{0.70\ \text{ha/hour}}=\$77.14/\text{ha}</formula></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">Method: <a href="https://www.extension.iastate.edu/agdm/crops/html/a3-24.html">Iowa State University Extension</a>.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="zZB1kjz0C4"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="7eYzNhFwdR" colspan="37"><h2>Efficiency is won across five stages</h2><grid divider="sm neutral-border" marker="number" marker-style="subtle" marker-shape="rounded" marker-position="inline" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" direction="vertical" vertical-sizing="fill" style="--marker-inline-size: 30pt; --marker-gap: 12pt;"><grid-item id="frX5rY5EuR" padding="8pt 0"><h4>Plan</h4><p>Map field shape, access and the available work window.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="7AEiIhFq-w" padding="8pt 0"><h4>Select</h4><p>Match implement, tractor power and expected utilization.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="DrRZP5_LM-" padding="8pt 0"><h4>Set up</h4><p>Calibrate width, depth, pressure and inputs.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="W0aAKJZsGO" padding="8pt 0"><h4>Operate</h4><p>Control speed, overlap, turns and refill waiting.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="chZDKDkLY6" padding="8pt 0"><h4>Verify</h4><p>Inspect quality, record losses and correct the next run.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="uvSWkeFG45" padding="0" colspan="23"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/hU_BGOK_LkZWEFWX1U_UO.png" saved-media-id="ji5pgphgd0ysctl" source="image.ai-generated" fill="true" image-style="technical-field-documentary" alt="Elevated documentary photograph of an unbranded tractor turning precisely at a field headland while input containers are staged beside the access lane, route geometry and waiting points visible, neutral overcast daylight, realistic soil and crop texture, white, carbon-black and machine-gray palette with restrained signal-red cones, no text, no logos, no identifiable people" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="slf79en9Qj"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="WAmTardMtT" padding="0" colspan="17"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/SyoKGYHsVqJ-nHsxCFQbb.png" saved-media-id="xu5ei3utf9l006e" source="image.ai-generated" fill="true" image-style="technical-field-documentary" alt="Close technical documentary photograph of gloved operator hands aligning an unbranded tractor hitch with a field implement, coupling points, hydraulic lines and working-width hardware clearly visible, neutral overcast daylight, machine-gray metal with one restrained signal-red safety detail, no text, no logos, no identifiable face" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item><grid-item id="_-YedioLbd" vertical-align="center" colspan="43"><p role="eyebrow">Illustrative options · same field task</p><h2>Select the system, not the biggest machine</h2><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="UAE08YXnQd" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><labels><label variant="outline">Option A</label></labels><h3>2.0 m system</h3><formula>2.0\times5.0\times0.70\div10=0.70</formula><p>Effective capacity, ha/hour</p><display size="md">$77.14<span font-size="18pt">/ha</span></display><formula>\$54/\text{hour}\div0.70=\$77.14/\text{ha}</formula></grid-item><grid-item id="Zb-c5zav0K" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><labels><label variant="solid">Option B · Conditional advantage</label></labels><h3>3.0 m system</h3><formula>3.0\times6.0\times0.75\div10=1.35</formula><p>Effective capacity, ha/hour</p><display size="md">$57.78<span font-size="18pt">/ha</span></display><formula>\$78/\text{hour}\div1.35=\$57.78/\text{ha}</formula></grid-item></grid><p><b>Select B only if power, hitch, soil load, transport width, access and annual use are acceptable.</b></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="AfZ89A3Jod" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="o8wl1mkOnd"><p role="eyebrow">Illustrative calculation · 12 ha · USD</p><h2>Reproduce the calculation</h2><p>Follow the units through each link. The effective capacity calculated in step three becomes the denominator for both cost figures.</p><grid marker="number" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-gap: 0.6em;"><grid-item id="3ArsRtp0x6" colspan="15"><h4>State the inputs</h4><p>Width 2.0 m; speed 5.0 km/h; efficiency 0.70; hourly cost $54.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="nM6KrQnELI" colspan="15"><h4>Find theoretical capacity</h4><formula>C_t=2.0\times5.0\div10=1.00</formula><p>ha/hour before field losses.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="1kHpsaGXQZ" colspan="15"><h4>Apply field efficiency</h4><formula>C_e=1.00\times0.70=0.70</formula><p>ha/hour effective capacity.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="vWBfIBT-cV" colspan="15"><h4>Convert capacity to cost</h4><formula>54\div0.70=77.14</formula><p>$77.14/ha</p><formula>54\times12\div0.70=925.71</formula><p>$925.71 for 12 ha.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">Cost method: <a href="https://www.extension.iastate.edu/agdm/crops/html/a3-29.html">Iowa State University Extension</a>. Illustrative USD; excludes taxes, financing terms, subsidies and policy effects.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="bE2cdYSGd-"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="4efX5HBpDy"><h2>Turn measured losses into actions</h2><p>Start with the observed signal, verify its cause, then change the part of the system that created the loss.</p><table col-widths="[23,35,42]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false"><tbody><tr><td background-color="surface"><p>Measured signal</p></td><td background-color="surface"><p>Verify the cause</p></td><td background-color="surface"><p>Action</p></td></tr><tr><td valign="middle"><p><span text-color="accent"><b>Low field efficiency</b></span></p></td><td valign="middle"><p>Time turns and refills.</p></td><td valign="middle"><p>Redesign routes and stage inputs before work begins.</p></td></tr><tr><td valign="middle"><p><span text-color="accent"><b>Low capacity</b></span></p></td><td valign="middle"><p>Check actual speed, working width and available power.</p></td><td valign="middle"><p>Correct the limiting mismatch; do not raise speed if quality or soil conditions deteriorate.</p></td></tr><tr><td valign="middle"><p><span text-color="accent"><b>High cost/ha</b></span></p></td><td valign="middle"><p>Inspect idle time, fuel, repairs and annual utilization.</p></td><td valign="middle"><p>Reduce avoidable idle hours and match ownership or hire cost to expected use.</p></td></tr><tr><td valign="middle"><p><span text-color="accent"><b>Poor work quality</b></span></p></td><td valign="middle"><p>Measure overlap, misses and depth.</p></td><td valign="middle"><p>Calibrate before increasing speed or capacity.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="sEfAIvfS9d" background-color="accent" padding="12pt 16pt"><p><b>Track together:</b> ha/hour, field efficiency, cost/ha, fuel/ha, downtime and work quality.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="-JNzizJ6IZ"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="ZRN3WYNYWl" padding="0" colspan="19"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/DhXm_2dZxwf7I543zrOu8.png" saved-media-id="uy5fwwdz6qhg3dg" source="image.ai-generated" fill="true" image-style="technical-field-documentary" alt="Elevated documentary photograph of an unbranded tractor approaching a field headland where inputs, tools and a support trailer have been staged in an orderly sequence, short turning path and reduced waiting geometry clearly visible, neutral overcast daylight, realistic soil texture, machine-gray equipment with restrained signal-red route markers, no text, no logos, no identifiable people" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item><grid-item id="9Rq0031qou" vertical-align="center" colspan="41"><p role="eyebrow">Illustrative case study · same 12 ha field</p><h2>Remove waiting before adding power</h2><p>Better headland routing and staged inputs raise assumed field efficiency from 0.70 to 0.82. Width, speed and the $54/hour cost remain unchanged.</p><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="0YoAz9EpCO" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><labels><label variant="outline">Before</label></labels><display size="md">0.70</display><h4>Efficiency → capacity</h4><p>0.70 ha/hour effective capacity</p><hr color="neutral-border"><p><b>17.14 hours</b><br>$77.14/ha<br>$925.71 total</p></grid-item><grid-item id="i-Z-mBtnVH" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><labels><label variant="solid">After</label></labels><display size="md">0.82</display><h4>Efficiency → capacity</h4><p>0.82 ha/hour effective capacity</p><hr color="neutral-border"><p><b>14.63 hours</b><br>$65.85/ha<br>$790.24 total</p></grid-item></grid><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="bxiOhvjIWs" background-color="accent" padding="12pt 16pt"><h3>2.51 hours and $135.47 saved</h3><p>14.6% less time and cost—without more width or power.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="wxmMrlIVmL" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="m50kqibFy8"><p role="eyebrow">Operating standard</p><h2>The field rule: measure, improve, remeasure</h2><smart-layout variant="cycle" cell-size="15"><smart-layout-item><icon class="accessory-image" src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/TntEzmEMZwRCgPTLV0Q7.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="field capacity measurement"></icon><div><h4>Measure</h4><p>Record effective capacity under real field conditions.</p></div></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><icon class="accessory-image" src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/ddct3Pc2TMCj5JrcoxFs72.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="stopwatch loss analysis"></icon><div><h4>Separate</h4><p>Isolate turning, waiting, adjustment and stoppage losses.</p></div></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><icon class="accessory-image" src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/ZWhniYkgDw7DgLalfnMM.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="agricultural machine comparison"></icon><div><h4>Compare</h4><p>Test viable machines in work-window hours and cost per hectare.</p></div></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><icon class="accessory-image" src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/eyvwP5lQKMl2gdbOvVdM.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="route calibration maintenance"></icon><div><h4>Improve first</h4><p>Fix routing, logistics, calibration and maintenance before adding capacity.</p></div></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><icon class="accessory-image" src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/ALwwg82HS65rdGuUK77Y.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="quality inspection repeat measurement"></icon><div><h4>Remeasure</h4><p>Check cost and work quality after every change.</p></div></smart-layout-item></smart-layout><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="ZvLToKcGwk" background-color="accent" padding="14pt 18pt"><h3>Which lost minute is cheapest to eliminate before buying more machine?</h3></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>